        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بحث کرنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بحث کرنا — bahas karnā — \"to argue; to debate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وہ دونوں ہر بات پر بحث کرتے ہیں۔ voh donoṅ har bāt par bahas karte haiṅ. Those two argue about everything."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے استاد سے بحث کی, us ne ustād se bahas kī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بحث کرنا (bahas karnā) is built from bahas, usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic baḥth, \"an inquiry, a discussion\", and کرنا, \"to do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
